ment, screen-clear, OSC title sequences, etc.) in the <!-- zbuild-holder: --> field. The sed pattern only strips CSI sequences ending in m or K; other ESC-prefixed sequences survive into _ZBUILD_CLAIM_HOLDER and are then sent to stderr via printf '%s\\\\n' \\\"${_ZBUILD_CLAIM_HOLDER:-unknown}\\\" >&2, where any terminal emulator will interpret them.\",\"accepted_if\":\"The holder string extracted from outside input is stripped of all ANSI/terminal escape sequences before being printed to stderr, using a strip that is at least as broad as the event bus's _eb_strip_ansi (which covers CSI sequences ending in any letter or ~ and bare ESC-X pairs).\",\"introduced\":true,\"fix\":\"code\"}]","files":{"/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/event-bus/event-bus.sh":"61462a1a2cdd0ba3cdf09591604fd78a7e9ac15f","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/pipeline/runner.sh":"640b4c0571bfe697f236a515f95be55b18d805f9","/home/runner/.claude/projects/-home-runner--zbuild-repos-ezigus-zBuild-issues-1764-worktree/b931d1d2-8493-47c3-9722-cfe3669ee647/tool-results/bhu53m6dj.txt":"ea9f07e55ebb11e1e64e149cf688b89e448f4d8a","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/claim/claim.sh":"707f8ea05518fe3845c2d8ef7b8912a5c2f36ccd","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/config/adr-enforcement-baseline.txt":"8f959db802864d3711fb73f512a6d2aa24c4859d","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/config/event-schema.json":"30dce672627cb047400df8eb0e095c14e8917247","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/docs/adr/ADR-005-claim-coordinator.md":"cb484550d5797621e2427cc2e122c3ba49b4697a","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/docs/adr/ADR-059-issue-vs-run-keying.md":"f9f9941985666c06510ecc46b5436b93fe3d20dc","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/README.md":"205a9ee2a2c256653e386